276
00:29:10,400 --> 00:29:12,960
You till the soil, water it, fertilize it.

277
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:15,840
You do everything you possibly can.

278
00:29:17,560 --> 00:29:20,000
But even if it grows up rotten…

279
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:23,000
you can't just pull it out by the roots.

280
00:29:23,800 --> 00:29:25,480
You just have to keep it as it is.

281
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:30,040
Maybe it's because

282
00:29:30,120 --> 00:29:31,840
the soil was too poor to begin with.

283
00:29:37,280 --> 00:29:38,720
Or maybe

284
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:42,040
the seed was already damaged
before it was ever planted.

285
00:29:42,920 --> 00:29:44,400
Put it in any soil,

286
00:29:44,960 --> 00:29:46,280
it would grow out the same.

287
00:29:54,560 --> 00:29:56,600
But Q doesn't seem anything
like Chee at all.

288
00:29:56,960 --> 00:29:59,280
You're from the same seed.

289
00:30:00,120 --> 00:30:02,240
You're my real nephew.

290
00:30:07,040 --> 00:30:09,240
If I could have you as a son…

291
00:30:10,520 --> 00:30:13,440
I think you'd protect
everything I've built.

292
00:30:14,640 --> 00:30:16,400
But Chee…

293
00:30:17,280 --> 00:30:19,760
he'd burn through every last bit of it.

294
00:30:46,960 --> 00:30:49,520
Hey, you remember that girl Noina
the one with the big tits?

295
00:30:49,960 --> 00:30:51,640
The one whose mom sells tofu milk?

296
00:30:51,720 --> 00:30:53,040
Yeah, her.

297
00:30:53,280 --> 00:30:56,040
So yesterday I went to buy some
around seven, when it's still busy.

298
00:30:56,120 --> 00:30:57,640
And besides the tofu milk…

299
00:30:57,720 --> 00:30:59,880
I got an eyeful of Noi's chest too.

300
00:31:00,320 --> 00:31:01,440
Always visiting there.

301
00:31:01,520 --> 00:31:02,520
Hey!

302
00:31:03,680 --> 00:31:05,240
I figured it must taste good,

303
00:31:05,320 --> 00:31:06,640
I see you there all the time.

304
00:31:06,720 --> 00:31:09,160
I can't even drink it.

305
00:31:09,920 --> 00:31:11,120
You're something else, you know that?

306
00:31:11,200 --> 00:31:14,280
Lean in a little, boing, boing, boing.

307
00:31:15,520 --> 00:31:16,520
Hey.

308
00:31:21,960 --> 00:31:23,760
Hey, Jeans from the butcher shop.

309
00:31:24,040 --> 00:31:25,280
Come drink with us!

310
00:31:27,080 --> 00:31:29,600
The butcher's niece, just moved here.

311
00:31:29,680 --> 00:31:30,720
She's insanely cute, bro.

312
00:31:32,080 --> 00:31:34,840
Chee will come for you
if you try anything.

313
00:31:35,280 --> 00:31:36,760
We've got grilled fish too, Jeans!

314
00:31:39,640 --> 00:31:40,800
Come hang with us, come on!

315
00:31:41,320 --> 00:31:42,560
Jeans!

316
00:31:45,400 --> 00:31:46,840
Stuck-up little…

317
00:31:50,600 --> 00:31:51,600
Chee,

318
00:31:52,640 --> 00:31:54,440
you've got a very clear type, man.

319
00:31:56,120 --> 00:31:59,160
Pan was cute, and Jeans is just
as cute as Pan.

320
00:31:59,400 --> 00:32:01,400
Bro, you are something else.

321
00:32:01,480 --> 00:32:03,760
Respect. Smooth.

322
00:32:04,320 --> 00:32:07,480
This area really
hasn't changed at all, has it.

323
00:32:08,560 --> 00:32:12,400
Three years ago it was like this

324
00:32:27,240 --> 00:32:28,600
Look around.

325
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:31,640
Once it starts getting dark,
people disappear.

326
00:32:31,840 --> 00:32:34,160
That's why you used to bring
Pan out here back then.

327
00:32:34,240 --> 00:32:35,800
The hell did you say?!

328
00:32:35,880 --> 00:32:38,320
Hey, Chee! Chee!

329
00:32:38,400 --> 00:32:40,080
Let me go!

330
00:32:40,160 --> 00:32:41,480
Let me go!

331
00:32:41,560 --> 00:32:42,640
What has gotten into you?

332
00:32:42,720 --> 00:32:44,520
Calm down, man!

333
00:32:44,600 --> 00:32:45,880
You wanna go, M?

334
00:32:45,960 --> 00:32:47,560
-What's it gonna be?
-You wanna go?

335
00:32:47,640 --> 00:32:48,640
What's wrong?

336
00:32:48,720 --> 00:32:49,760
Chee, calm down.

337
00:32:49,840 --> 00:32:51,200
You wanna go, too?

338
00:32:51,280 --> 00:32:52,280
Calm down!

339
00:32:53,480 --> 00:32:54,720
Dammit!

340
00:32:55,880 --> 00:32:56,880
Let go!

341
00:32:57,480 --> 00:32:59,440
I'm not eating any damn fish now!

342
00:33:01,160 --> 00:33:02,680
Don't you have other things to say?

343
00:33:02,760 --> 00:33:03,920
You scum!

344
00:33:14,800 --> 00:33:17,600
Come on.

345
00:33:35,440 --> 00:33:38,360
Dammit. Where is it?

346
00:33:40,880 --> 00:33:41,920
What the hell?

347
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:43,000
Mom,

348
00:33:43,080 --> 00:33:44,400
what's going on?

349
00:33:45,080 --> 00:33:46,320
What are you finding?

350
00:33:46,880 --> 00:33:51,040
Hey.
Have you seen Pan's blouse?

351
00:33:51,120 --> 00:33:55,480
The red one,
with the butterfly in the middle.

352
00:33:55,560 --> 00:33:57,400
Pan's blouse.
Have you seen it?

353
00:33:58,600 --> 00:33:59,800
It's been so long now.

354
00:33:59,880 --> 00:34:01,080
What do you need it for, Mom?

355
00:34:01,160 --> 00:34:03,520
Ugh, don't ask so many questions.

356
00:34:05,160 --> 00:34:06,320
Mom had a dream about Pan,

357
00:34:06,760 --> 00:34:08,240
she said she was cold.

358
00:34:13,040 --> 00:34:15,560
I can't find anything.

359
00:34:15,960 --> 00:34:17,160
Mom.

360
00:34:18,280 --> 00:34:20,160
you're very drunk. Do you realise that?

361
00:34:23,320 --> 00:34:25,520
-Why is everything such a mess in here?
-Mom.

362
00:34:25,600 --> 00:34:29,600
-Ugh, I can't find it!
-That's enough. I'll help you look later!

363
00:34:31,120 --> 00:34:32,320
Umm.

364
00:34:35,200 --> 00:34:36,720
You think I'm crazy, don't you.

365
00:34:38,280 --> 00:34:39,320
No No.

366
00:34:39,680 --> 00:34:41,040
You think I'm crazy, don't you?

367
00:34:41,120 --> 00:34:42,160
It's not like that, Mom!

368
00:34:42,240 --> 00:34:44,080
Don't give me that!
You're lying!

369
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:46,720
You hate your sister.

370
00:34:47,960 --> 00:34:50,560
You think she's dead,
just like everyone else thinks.

371
00:34:51,800 --> 00:34:52,960
You're a bad person.

372
00:34:53,360 --> 00:34:55,600
You don't love me!
You don't love your own sister!

373
00:34:55,680 --> 00:34:57,360
-You wicked child!
-Ugh!

374
00:34:57,440 --> 00:34:59,400
What do you mean I don't love you?

375
00:34:59,480 --> 00:35:01,200
She's not coming back, Mom!

376
00:35:01,280 --> 00:35:02,320
Shut your mouth.

377
00:35:04,160 --> 00:35:05,680
Pan is coming back.

378
00:35:11,720 --> 00:35:13,240
I still can't find anything!

379
00:35:20,520 --> 00:35:22,000
Is this what you were looking for?

380
00:35:25,440 --> 00:35:26,720
I've worn it so many times already,

381
00:35:26,800 --> 00:35:28,000
Mom. You never even noticed.

382
00:35:31,520 --> 00:35:32,720
That's all I asked!

383
00:36:43,240 --> 00:36:44,360
Then we ride.

384
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:46,600
Follow me,

385
00:36:46,680 --> 00:36:48,360
I'll take you to see something.

386
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:01,000
Pan.

387
00:37:01,080 --> 00:37:02,560
Go, go.

388
00:37:08,840 --> 00:37:10,200
Pan.

389
00:37:31,280 --> 00:37:32,600
Nai?

390
00:37:33,160 --> 00:37:35,160
M? Joe?

391
00:38:37,400 --> 00:38:38,880
Who is it?

392
00:38:39,720 --> 00:38:40,920
Come out.

393
00:38:53,920 --> 00:38:55,000
Pan!

394
00:39:20,280 --> 00:39:21,400
Pan.

395
00:39:27,880 --> 00:39:29,080
Pan.
